    "message": "Load the head checkpoint once when a computation starts\n\nPressing compute decoded the whole head checkpoint three times before\nthe first tick: submit() loaded it to check the target range, the worker\nloaded it to read the LLM settings, and _advance_locked loaded it again.\nEach load_branch also re-validated what load_checkpoint had just\nvalidated. submit() now bounds the target with the branch pointer and\nthe Scenario duration, the worker reads only the pointer and\nruntime_state, and load_branch no longer validates twice. Creating a\nchild branch reads only the parent's pointer.\n\nA corrupt head is still rejected, now by the worker, which marks the\nrun failed and leaves the branch pointer unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
